# DuckDB CLI upstream pin.
#
# DuckDB ships **precompiled single-file CLI binaries** — our build
# scripts download the right per-platform archive from GitHub Releases
# rather than building from source. Same shape as the uv pin, and for
# the same reason: no upstream clone, no commit-sha-driven checkout,
# just a tag plus per-archive sha256 digests.
#
# Unlike uv, DuckDB publishes no companion `.sha256` files, so the
# digests below are computed from the downloaded archives themselves.
#
# The `commit=` field is the sha the tag points at — used by the shared
# preflight in .github/workflows/build-native.yml to decide whether the
# engine is pinned (non-zero sha) or skippable (all zeros). It is also
# echoed by `duckdb --version`, which is how the build script's smoke
# test confirms it extracted the binary it pinned.
#
# How to bump:
#   1. `gh api repos/duckdb/duckdb/releases/latest --jq .tag_name`
#   2. `gh api repos/duckdb/duckdb/git/refs/tags/<tag> --jq .object.sha`
#   3. For each platform archive, download it and hash it:
#      `curl -sSL https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/releases/download/<tag>/<asset> | shasum -a 256`
#   4. Run `./build.sh` locally to validate, then tag `native-vX.Y.Z`.
#
# The glibc (non-musl) Linux archives are pinned deliberately, matching
# the rest of the native tree.
#
# License: MIT (https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb)
upstream=https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb
tag=v1.5.5
commit=d8cdaa33fda8df955cc76ef58a280f68f4cd43fa

# Per-platform archive sha256 digests, computed from the release assets.
# If these drift, the build script's verification fails loudly at
# download time.
